# AirSkyBoat

FFXI server emulator (LandSandBoat fork). Era accuracy: `modules/era/`. Live-server QoL: `modules/custom/`.

If you are an AI agent, read `documentation/ai_agents/README.md` first. Style: [LSB Development Guide](https://github.com/LandSandBoat/server/wiki/Development-Guide). Workflow: [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/LandSandBoat/server/blob/base/CONTRIBUTING.md).

## Remotes

- `origin` → live fork (`LIVE` / FFXI_server-v2). Do not open LSB PRs from here.
- `upstream` → `LandSandBoat/server` (`base`).
- `lsb-fork` → `JasonW77/lsb-server` for upstream PR branches.

## Live fork flavor

- **75 cap**, **no Abyssea**. Live story QoL through **Nations → RoZ → CoP → ToAU → WoTG → ACP/AMK/ASA**.
- Out of scope for live flavor unless asked: **RoV, SoA, TVR, Abyssea**.
- **Mog Satchel** is intentionally disabled on Live (`char_storage.satchel` default 0, no OTP). Do not re-enable unless asked. Wardrobe/inventory QoL is separate (`custom-module` skill).
- `modules/init.txt` may be **committed on `LIVE`** for deploy (pull on live usually enables new module lines). **Never** include `init.txt` in LandSandBoat upstream PRs (`lsb-fork`). Edit live `init.txt` by hand only when pull is blocked by local drift or the user asks (`ssh-live` skill).

## Do

- Copy nearby scripts for syntax, enums, and formatting. Ask when retail behavior is unclear.
- Prefer Interaction Framework for new quest/mission NPC logic.
- Cite sources in code comments or commit messages (wiki, captures, SE posts, patch dates). PR text is not enough.
- Put live-server QoL in `modules/custom/` and enable it in `modules/init.txt` (`custom/lua/foo.lua`). OK on `LIVE`; never in LSB upstream PRs.
- Prefer small, focused changes. Ask before large rewrites or IF migrations.
- Before an LSB PR, diff against current `upstream/base`, not `LIVE`. Search GitHub for an existing core fix first.
- Keep LSB commit **subject ≤ 72 characters** (CI Sanity Checks fails otherwise).
- Fishing is **C++ + SQL** (`src/map/utils/fishingutils.cpp`, `sql/fishing_*.sql`); disabled by default (`FISHING_ENABLE`). Not a Lua or `modules/custom/` feature.

## Do not

- Invent FFXI mechanics, timings, event IDs, drops, job math, message IDs, or item animations.
- Rely on wiki alone for message IDs, animation IDs, or fail-path packets. Leave those unverified / TODO until a retail packet exists.
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` (or other agent trailers). Prefer **disabling** Cursor Attribution so it is not injected: Cursor Settings → Git & PRs (or Agent) → Attribution off, and `~/.cursor/cli-config.json` with `attribution.attributeCommitsToAgent` / `attributePRsToAgent` false (`update-cursor-settings` skill). If a trailer still appears, strip before push: write the filtered message to a file, then `git commit --amend -F <file>` — do **not** pipe the filter alone into `-F -` (junk message) and do **not** rely on `| amend -F -` on PowerShell (often re-injects). **Verify** `git log -1 --format=%B` has no trailer. Recipes: `lsb-pr` skill (PowerShell tempfile + `filter-branch`). Strip on `LIVE` pushes too.
- Use DarkStar (`dsp.*`), Windower, or unrelated Lua addon patterns. Match this tree.
- Put non-retail QoL in `scripts/` or `modules/era/` (example: HELM yield multipliers belong in `modules/custom/`).
- Treat `scripts/zones/**/IDs.lua` numeric shifts as “drive-by formatting.” On this live client they may be intentional DAT/message offsets (boxes/item text). Ask before reverting.
- Rename `npc_list` internal names to match stale scripts after a client dump. Retarget IF / `DefaultActions` / `npcs` to the dump names instead (`npc-scripts` skill).
- Convert old NPC scripts to IF without captures and wiki triangulation.
- Edit `settings/*.lua` except `settings/default/` (local settings are gitignored).
- Touch `ext/` or `dev.docker-compose.yml` unless asked (copy Compose changes to `docker-compose.yml`).
- Commit secrets, `tools/config.yaml`, `sql/backups/`, or live DB dumps. Do not commit `init.txt` to **LSB upstream PRs**; per-environment entries belong on `LIVE` or local only.
- Publish exploit details in issues/PRs/chat; flag them privately.
- Deploy, pull, or restart the live map process unless asked. Use the personal `ssh-live` skill.

## Verify

Mark unverified or 1-to-1 conversion work in comments. Remind the user to check the game client, retail captures, `../FFXI-EventsDump`, BG-Wiki, and FFXIclopedia.
